<title>USA: World Bank's Frank to leave for private sector.</title>
<headline>World Bank's Frank to leave for private sector.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The World Bank said on Monday that Managing Director Richard Frank will leave the lending agency in June.</p>
<p>Frank, 56, will be joining Darby Overseas Investment Ltd, an investment company that specializes in emerging markets and which is headed by former Treasury Secretary Nicholas Brady.</p>
<p>A 27-year veteran of the World Bank group, Frank played a key role in promoting the private sector in developing countries, including an eight-year stint at the lending agency's International Finance Corp affiliate.</p>
